M131-stderr-pipe                       corpus_equal=1 selftest_identical=1 (n=12)
   proof: stderr=PIPE vs DEVNULL changes nothing observable: the journalctl stub writes nothing to stderr; the parent never reads the pipe; child exit status identical. Divergence would require a stub that fills stderr before EOF on stdout (not in any fixture).
M132-expect-dups-not-deduped           corpus_equal=1 selftest_identical=1 (n=12)
   proof: report() re-applies set() to `expects` (`missing = sorted(set(e for e in expects ...))`), so removal of the dedup in run() leaves every output byte unchanged.
